    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "## What changed\n\n`machine::judge::move_extremes` gives the points that the machine travel check judges for one move.\nFor an arc, it now gives the two endpoints and only the quarter points that the arc sweeps.\nThe sweep runs from `from` to `to` in the direction of `arc.ccw`, in the arc's own plane (XY, XZ or YZ).\nThe mill, lathe, plasma, waterjet and wire checks all read this one function.\n\nThe check keeps all four quarter points in two cases:\n\n- The in-plane endpoints are 0.01 mm apart or less. Their NC words can be equal, and a control turns equal endpoints a full circle.\n- The sweep reads zero or is not finite.\n\nA four-decimal inch post has a 0.00254 mm step on each axis.\nEndpoints less than 0.0036 mm apart can round to the same point on a diagonal.\nThe 0.01 mm bound includes margin and agrees with `ring_zig::MIN_ARC_CHORD`.\n\nThe radius is now the larger of the two endpoint radii. The old code used the radius at `from`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe old function added all four quarter points of the arc's full circle.\nA 2D Contour cuts a gentle curve as an arc with a very large radius.\nThe issue's move 31 has a radius of 22170 mm and a sweep of 0.259 degrees.\nThe check judged points 22 m away from the tool and refused a legal program on each machine size.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/machine_arc_sweep.rs` (9 tests). It runs `machine::check_ops` on one cached move.\n\n- `a_shallow_arc_of_a_large_radius_inside_the_stroke_passes`\n- `the_same_endpoints_the_long_way_round_are_refused_on_their_own_side`\n- `an_arc_is_judged_on_the_side_that_it_sweeps`\n- `a_vertical_plane_arc_is_judged_on_the_side_that_it_sweeps`\n- `a_quarter_point_on_an_endpoint_counts`\n- `a_full_circle_keeps_all_four_quarter_points`\n- `endpoints_that_post_as_one_point_keep_all_four_quarter_points`\n- `endpoints_that_round_to_one_inch_point_keep_all_four_quarter_points`\n- `an_arc_with_no_sweep_to_read_keeps_all_four_quarter_points`\n\nOriginal evidence before the review fix: 4 of the original 8 tests fail on the code of `upstream/main` (the shallow arc, the two side tests, the no-sweep arc). The failure of the shallow arc shows the issue's symptom: `move 0 reaches 22320.200 in X, the stroke is -3000.000..3000.000`.\n\nOriginal mutation results (each mutation restored, then the original suite is green, 8 of 8):\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Old `judge.rs` from `upstream/main` | red: 4 tests fail |\n| Remove the 0.001 mm endpoint guard | red: `endpoints_that_post_as_one_point_keep_all_four_quarter_points` |\n| Remove the zero-sweep guard | red: `an_arc_with_no_sweep_to_read_keeps_all_four_quarter_points` |\n| Ignore `arc.ccw` | red: the three side tests |\n\nReview fix evidence: `endpoints_that_round_to_one_inch_point_keep_all_four_quarter_points` passes with `SAME_WORD = 0.01`.\nReverting only `SAME_WORD` to 0.001 makes this test fail with `MachineCheck { problems: [] }`.\nRestoring 0.01 makes the test pass again.\n\nReview fix gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green.\nAll four steps pass: app build, app lib, `fourth_axis_pose`, and `machine_arc_sweep`.\nReview fix clippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nOriginal gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (app lib, `fourth_axis_pose`, `machine_arc_sweep`).\nThese suites are green too: `vmc_stroke`, `machine`, `lathe_stroke`, `lathe_thread_travel`, `plasma_machine`, `waterjet_machine`, `edm_machine`.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The reporter's project file. The tests use the radius, chord and stroke from the issue's table.\n- A full generate-and-post run of a 2D Contour with large-radius arcs.\n- The 1e-9 rad slack at an endpoint has no mutation test. The endpoint itself is always judged, so no output shows the slack alone.\n- A wire or lathe program with an arc that sweeps one side only. Their existing suites are green.\n- The wire suites other than `edm_machine` were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR changes `crates/app/src/machine/judge.rs`.\nIssue #2585 will move `judge.rs` to `camcraft-post`. The PR that merges second refreshes.\nIssue #1882 reads `move_extremes` for program bounds. This PR does not change it.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/2710-arc-swept-extremes.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The machine travel check judges only the points that an arc sweeps, so a shallow arc of a large radius inside the stroke posts (#2710).\n\nFixes #2710\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
